{"id":"H8496","lemma":"תֹּךְ","transliteration":"tokh","sayIt":"tokh","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"noun, masculine","gloss":"oppression","meaning":"1) injury, oppression, oppressor\n2) (TWOT) fraud, deceit, deceitful\nAlso means: ta.khakh (תָּכָךְ \"deceitful\" H8501)","glosses":["oppression","violence","oppressor"],"count":4,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"psa-10","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"and violence","kjv":"and fraud"}},{"chapterId":"psa-55","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"oppression","kjv":"deceit"}},{"chapterId":"psa-72","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"from oppression","kjv":"from deceit"}},{"chapterId":"pro-29","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"and the oppressor"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Psalm 10:7","note":"His mouth is full of cursing, deceit, and oppression. Under his tongue is mischief and iniquity.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Proverbs 29:13","note":"The poor man and the oppressor have this in common: Yahweh gives sight to the eyes of both.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H8501","lemma":"תָּכָךְ","transliteration":"takhakh","gloss":"deceitful"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}